The notes about "variance fixed to .001" should not be a problem, so long as the variance of each of your variables is not close to 0.

The other warnings say that the model did not converge. The first thing I would do is consider the prior distributions that you are using by looking at the dpriors(target = "jags") command. Those are fairly uninformative, and I would tailor those priors to be mildly informative for your dataset. Some further information is here:

https://ecmerkle.github.io/blavaan/articles/prior.html

Ed

